course: dictionary
lesson: 11361
title: Aah! A sound that shows feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Aah» is a small word, but it works in a special way. It is an interjection, a sound that bursts out to show how you feel. You can also spell it «ah» or «ahh».
explain: Context tells you which feeling it shows. «Aah, that's better» said after a warm bath shows relief. «Aah, now I see!» shows you have suddenly understood something. Read the words around it to decide.
explain: The doctor's «Open wide and say aah» is different. There you make the sound on purpose, so the doctor can look at your throat. The same word has a different job here.
explain: The number of a's shows how long the sound lasts. «Aaaah» is a long, slow sound, while «ah» is quick. Listen for the length when you read it aloud.
fact: «Aah» is an interjection: a sound word that shows a feeling.
fact: It can show relief, pleasure, calm, or sudden understanding.
fact: People make this sound at something sweet, like a baby or a kitten.
fact: A doctor may ask you to say «aah» so they can see your throat.
fact: The spellings «ah» and «ahh» mean the same sound; more a's means a longer sound.
exercise: «Aah, that's better,» said Mia, sinking into the warm bath. What feeling does «aah» show? | Anger | *Relief | Hunger | Surprise at a loud noise
exercise: «Aah, now I see!» said Sam, when the puzzle piece finally fitted. What does «aah» show here? | Sadness | A sore throat | Being cold | *Sudden understanding
exercise: The doctor said, «Open wide and say aah.» Why does the doctor want you to say aah? | So they can hear your favourite song | *So they can see your throat | To show you are sleepy | To tell you it is time for lunch
test: «Aah, look at the tiny kitten!» said Ella. What feeling does the sound show? | *Pleasure at something sweet | Fear of a dog | Anger at the rain | Boredom
test: Which is another spelling of aah? | *Ah | Eek | Ooh | Oi
exam: «Aaaah, the ice cream is so cold and lovely,» said Ben. What does the long «Aaaah» tell you? | It means stop | It is a word for a dog | *The sound is drawn out, showing a strong feeling | The sound is short and sharp
